PR review on Airwhale/Parea

Review comment:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The `switch` statement in `xtraceStatusToBeliefStatus` does not have a `default` case. If the upstream XTrace API introduces a new status in the future, this function will return `undefined`. Since `BeliefSchema` requires `status` to be one of `"active" | "revised" | "retracted"`, returning `undefined` will cause `BeliefSchema.parse` to throw a runtime validation error.

Adding a `default` case that maps unknown statuses to a safe fallback (like `"active"`) makes the integration more resilient.

```suggestion
const xtraceStatusToBeliefStatus = (
  record: XTraceMemoryRecord,
): Belief["status"] => {
  if (record.type !== "fact") {
    return "active";
  }

  switch (record.details.status) {
    case "retracted":

