PR review on bsorenson23-debug/lt316-admin-layout-

Review comment:
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The non-null assertion operator `!` is used on `derivedRevolveInput` when returning the object. We can avoid this unsafe assertion by adding an explicit null check right before returning, which also helps TypeScript narrow the type automatically.

```typescript
  if (runtimeQa.sourceContourHash !== lockedContourHash) {
    throw new Error("BODY REFERENCE GLB Stage 3C locked contour hash is stale relative to the accepted BODY REFERENCE locked source profile.");
  }

  if (!derivedRevolveInput) {
    throw new Error("BODY REFERENCE GLB Stage 3C requires locked Stage 3B revolve input metadata.");
  }

  return {
    runtimeQa,
    revolveInput: derivedRevolveInput,
  };
```

